---
import { evidenceUrl, url } from "../lib/specs";
const milestones = [
  { status: "Verified on hardware", title: "The ESP SDR demo works", text: "The user-operated live viewer delivered 2,706 verified frames over 60 seconds. Two earlier minutes also passed. Each restored and verified the original 4 MiB firmware. The localhost viewer closes before restoration.", proof: "docs/evidence/esp-demo-play-001/README.md", label: "Interactive demo and restoration", kind: "verified" },
  { status: "Fresh reception reproduced", title: "An owned BLE packet decoded", text: "Earlier matched controls decoded one fresh ten-bit/manual48 packet. The new eight-bit control has 1,260 intact snapshots and no CRC-valid packet. The ten-bit/manual control has 1,010 intact snapshots, three other-source CRC-valid packets and none from our source. Full restorations pass. The manual eight-bit trial failed a short read; the BW20/hardware condition completed 1,257 intact snapshots with no CRC-valid packet. The final BW12 condition completed 1,151 intact captures, independently verified with zero CRC-valid packets and full restoration. Detection rate remains unproved.", proof: "docs/evidence/ble-bluez-control-004/README.md", label: "Current ladder control and measured plot", kind: "verified" },
  { status: "Controller-count condition verified", title: "100 controller events and cleanup verified", text: "The source and monitor agree on 100 completed extended-advertising events. Normal monitor completion and cleanup pass. A separate primary-header decoder now passes 89 host checks; its reception remains unverified. Auxiliary-channel AD supplies no legacy RF hit rate.", proof: "docs/evidence/ble-primary-preparation/README.md", label: "Primary preparation and count limits", kind: "partial" },
  { status: "Verified on hardware", title: "RTL-SDR delivers useful reception", text: "The attached dipole received FM/RDS identifying WXJC. The receiver comparison is accepted; calibrated shared-signal sensitivity remains deferred.", proof: "docs/evidence/rtl-dipole-rds/README.md", label: "Current-dipole RDS proof", kind: "verified" },
  { status: "Production coordinator prepared", title: "Forgix gateware and its RP bridge build", text: "Configuration003 uses 203,700 SRAM bytes; register-only011 uses 28,868. UID initialization now follows watchdog enable and checks the ROM result. Nineteen coordinator and 23 backend checks pass. The coordinator retains a durable session lease and verifies recovery. A separate finite FIFO/source passes 34 peer-replayed tests and five actual-HDL probes; C/Python codecs pass 16 author and six independent groups. Attempt002 failed project verification and missed 32 MHz setup by 0.694 ns. The fresh third build passes artifact and exact XML verification; resources fit, but setup misses by 1.763 ns. The deadline change did not improve routed timing. A countdown scheduler is under evaluation. No FPGA was programmed. The registry remains empty; independent source and artifact review passes, while attachment and physical qualification precede loading.", proof: "docs/evidence/forgix-synthetic-compiler/README.md", label: "Three compiler attempts and timing limits", kind: "prepared" },
  { status: "64 KiB/s passes · 256 KiB/s loses data", title: "Forgix USB loss is measured", text: "The 64 KiB/s condition passes without loss. At requested 256 KiB/s, 15,530,520 payload bytes arrived over 60 seconds and 431 records were discarded, all accounted for. Full original-flash and factory verification passed. Maximum capacity and FPGA transport remain open.", proof: "docs/evidence/forgix-usb-ram-recovery/README.md", label: "USB measurements and retained failures", kind: "partial" },
];
---
<section class="project-checkpoint" aria-labelledby="checkpoint-title" data-project-checkpoint>
  <header><p class="eyebrow">CURRENT CHECKPOINT · OCTOBER 4, 2026</p><h2 id="checkpoint-title">The demo works. The next experiments have clear gates.</h2><p>Hardware results, software preparation and failed experiments are shown separately. The full RF and FPGA evaluations remain open.</p></header>
  <div class="milestones">{milestones.map(item => <article class={`milestone ${item.kind}`}><span class="milestone-status">{item.status}</span><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.text}</p><a href={evidenceUrl(item.proof)}>{item.label} →</a></article>)}</div>
  <div class="next-work"><div><p class="eyebrow">NEXT, IN ORDER</p><ol><li><strong>Finish FPGA timing and stream preparation.</strong> Prove countdown scheduling against the current HDL and rerun the unchanged 32 MHz constraint. Complete RP firmware and host collector reviews. Then re-establish the matching attachment and qualify board parameters and pin timing. The implemented coordinator requires a committed qualification before loading. Verify physical configuration and register readback. Earlier full preservation passes; refresh it before loading; physical FPGA transport is untested.</li><li><strong>Advance controlled ESP reception.</strong> The current eight-bit/BW12/hardware control remains null. The eight-bit/BW20/manual48 condition failed a short UART read and restored correctly. The BW20/hardware condition also remains null. Reviewed prefix retention and caller integration pass. The final original BW12 condition completed 1,151 intact captures with a null decoder/scalar result and verified restoration. Original Trial B stays gated; source-only controller counts supply no confirmed air denominator.</li><li><strong>Diagnose USB stalls and buffering.</strong> Use retained queue and loss timing before declaring another condition. The 256 KiB/s loss does not establish a USB ceiling; prepare the separate finite FPGA FIFO/source and autonomous RP/host path, then measure it before RF integration.</li></ol></div><aside><h3>What we need from you</h3><p>The latest USB survey finds the ESP and RTL-SDR, but no Forgix matching its preserved identity. Earlier full preservation and factory return remain valid historical evidence. A matching attachment is needed for further FPGA measurements; no ESP wiring is needed for the first internal register test. Your photos are received and your S31 remains backordered. The photos show the nominal 32 MHz oscillator marking. The small FPGA chip’s T8F49 suffix is still unreadable; grade, actual clock and pin timing need qualification.</p><h3>Will Forgix need wires to the ESP?</h3><p>The proposed direct path needs verified SPI I/O and a common ground. Forgix keeps USB to the PC. A PC-mediated processing demo is another option, but keeps ESP capture gaps. No inter-board wiring is needed for the current USB test.</p><a href={url("fpga/")}>Transport stages and pin ownership →</a></aside></div>
</section>
<style>
  .project-checkpoint { margin:2.5rem 0; padding:1.6rem; border:1px solid var(--rule); border-radius:12px; background:var(--surface); color:var(--ink); }
  header { max-width:64rem; margin-bottom:1.4rem; }
  h2 { font-size:clamp(1.5rem,2.7vw,2.2rem); line-height:1.15; margin:.5rem 0 .8rem; }
  header p, article p, aside p, li { color:var(--ink-2); line-height:1.55; }
  .milestones { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:1rem; }
  .milestone { padding:1.1rem; border:1px solid var(--rule); border-top:3px solid var(--accent); border-radius:7px; }
  .partial { border-top-color:var(--unverified); }
  .prepared { border-top-color:var(--muted); }
  .milestone-status { font: .65rem var(--mono); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.05em; color:var(--muted); }
  h3 { font-size:1.08rem; line-height:1.25; margin:.65rem 0; }
  article p { font-size:.9rem; margin:.7rem 0 1rem; }
  a { color:var(--accent); font-size:.88rem; }
  .next-work { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.45fr 1fr; gap:2rem; margin-top:1.5rem; padding-top:1.4rem; border-top:1px solid var(--rule); }
  ol { padding-left:1.2rem; margin:.7rem 0 0; }
  li { margin:.65rem 0; font-size:.92rem; }
  aside { padding:1rem 1.2rem; background:var(--surface-2); border-radius:7px; }
  aside h3:first-child { margin-top:0; }
  aside p { font-size:.9rem; }
  @media(max-width:1050px) { .milestones { grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); } }
  @media(max-width:650px) { .project-checkpoint { padding:1rem; } .milestones,.next-work { grid-template-columns:1fr; } .next-work { gap:1rem; } }
</style>
